FLEET HOME MARKER — read by Agent-One/hooks/routing_footer_check.py

Presence of this file, in the directory a session was launched from or within six ancestors of it,
puts that session inside the routing-footer hook's scope. The hook reads existence only; content is
for humans. It is WARN mode and never blocks.

WHY IT EXISTS HERE: this repository is Agent-Velo's boot folder. Every session of this agent — both
roles — launches from here and not from the fleet repo, so without this marker the hook was scoped to
a directory this home never stands in.

WHY A FILE AND NOT A LIST: the marker is opt-in by the home, placed in its own repo at its own
landing, so scope rides the landing cycle instead of arriving as a broadcast. An absent marker means
"this home has not landed the layer yet", never "this is not a fleet home".

PLACED: 2026-08-12, Navigator-42, on Agent-One's PROMPT №172, copying the shape of the reference
instance at `D:/02_Projects/aivis.one/Agent/.fleet-home` rather than inventing one.

⚠ NOTE FOR WHOEVER READS THIS NEXT: the companion half of that landing — the
`autoMemoryDirectory` key pointing at `C:/Users/AIVIS/.claude/fleet-memory` — lives in
`.claude/settings.local.json`, which this repository does NOT commit. This file is committable and
that one is not, which is exactly why the recovery text for the key is written into the agent home's
own board as well. If auto-memory ever looks empty in this repo, that key is the first thing to
check.
